/*!
\page page_stmtdrawhit StMtdRawHit

\brief Raw TDC hit from the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD) DAQ stream.

\section mtdrawhit_overview Overview

StMtdRawHit stores a single raw TDC hit from the MTD DAQ stream before any calibration.
Each object corresponds to one TDC edge (leading or trailing) recorded by the HPTDC electronics
on a given MTD backleg fiber.

The MTD became fully operational in Run 12 (2012) and uses the same TDIG/HPTDC electronics chain
as the BTOF; StMtdRawHit mirrors the structure of \ref StBTofRawHit, with "tray" replaced by "backleg".

The edge type is encoded in the sign of \c mFlag (positive = leading, negative = trailing);
the magnitude minus one gives the fiber ID.

Raw hits are stored in \ref StMtdCollection via StEvent::mtdCollection().

\section mtdrawhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StMtdRawHit
\endcode

\section mtdrawhit_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mFlag | Char_t | Edge flag: +ve = leading, −ve = trailing; \|flag\|−1 = fiberId |
| mBackLeg | UChar_t | Backleg number (1–30) |
| mChannel | UChar_t | TDC channel number |
| mTdc | UInt_t | Raw TDC count (~24.4 ps/bin) |

\section mtdrawhit_methods Key Methods

- flag() — raw flag byte
- leadingEdge() — true if leading-edge hit
- trailingEdge() — true if trailing-edge hit
- fiberId() — fiber ID (0-based)
- backleg() — backleg number (1–30)
- channel() — TDC channel number
- tdc() — raw TDC count

\section mtdrawhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StMtdCollection* coll = event->mtdCollection();
if (coll) {
    const StSPtrVecMtdRawHit& rawHits = coll->mtdRawHits();
    for (const auto& r : rawHits) {
        int  backleg = r->backleg();
        int  chan    = r->channel();
        bool isLE   = r->leadingEdge();
        int  fiber  = r->fiberId();
        double approxNs = r->tdc() * 24.4e-3; // [ns]
    }
}
\endcode

\see StMtdHit, StMtdHeader, StMtdCollection, StBTofRawHit
*/
